\caption(Explicit five-epoch Adam fit and a tensor-computed true/predicted-class count matrix at the selected checkpoint. Training uses augmentation and batch BN moments; validation/test use saved moving moments. Counts sum to 32; IDs follow the original CIFAR-10 order. The title gives the colour limits.)
\alttext(Explicit five-epoch Adam fit and a tensor-computed true/predicted-class count matrix at the selected checkpoint. Training uses augmentation and batch BN moments; validation/test use saved moving moments. Counts sum to 32; IDs follow the original CIFAR-10 order. The title gives the colour limits.)


The half-width fit selects epoch four: validation NLL 2.325037, inference
training NLL 2.159872, test NLL 2.470615 and accuracy 6.25% (2 of 32). After
20 updates it does not generalise beyond chance (NLL ln 10 ≈ 2.30) on this small
held-out subset. The training trace uses batch moments and augmentation; the
held-out NLL is measured with the saved inference moments instead. The identity-path checks
establish their algebraic claim independently of this unsuccessful short fit.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/preactivation_resnet_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Removing the post-add gate makes the raw equal-width shortcut an exact signed identity when
the residual is zero. Projections have a different preactivated input and need separate checks.
Complete-depth counts, gradients and the explicit half-width subset fit preserve those rules
without claiming that the short run reproduces the released training results.

> References

- [He et al. (2016), Identity Mappings in Deep Residual Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05027).
- [Released CIFAR pre-activation implementation](https://github.com/KaimingHe/resnet-1k-layers/blob/master/resnet-pre-act.lua).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset and binary-file format](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
